{
  "requirement": "Each assessment’s usage record MUST include its total failed provider attempts and retries, including failures recovered by a successful retry. A terminal failure MUST retain the accumulated counts.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover both obligations in `requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`.\n\n**Obligation 1: the usage record includes total failed attempts and retries, including failures recovered by a successful retry.**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt]` covers the recovered case. The provider fails 5 times with 429 and then succeeds. The persisted usage log asserts `provider_usage.failed_attempts == 5`, `retries == 5` and `attempts == 6`. It also asserts that each of the five failed requests records a failure with status, code and `retried: true`, and that the final completed request has no failure.\n- `src/authoring/usage.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt]` checks per-request failure recording at the usage-log level. A failed request records status and code with `retried: false`. After `retried()` is called, the persisted value becomes `true`. A later successful request raises `request_count` to 2.\n\n**Obligation 2: a terminal failure retains the accumulated counts.**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[a_request_failing_for_a_minute_fails_the_assessment]` covers retry exhaustion. After N attempts, the persisted log has `attempts == N`, `failed_attempts == N` and `retries == N-1`. The last request is recorded with `retried == false`.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[permanent_provider_failure_returns_without_waiting_or_retrying]` covers a permanent failure. The log has `attempts == 1`, `failed_attempts == 1` and `retries == 0`.\n- `cancelling_during_backoff_prevents_another_request` also asserts `failed_attempts == 1` and `retries == 0` on the in-memory usage record. I used it only as supporting evidence.\n\n**Supporting tests.**\n- `src/authoring/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failure_codes_are_the_status_and_code_a_provider_reports]` and `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sdk_string_errors_preserve_habeas_provider_reports_and_error_kinds]` verify extraction of the status and code that the failure records carry.\n\n**Result.** The distinct scenarios the text governs are all tested, and the assertions check the counts on the persisted log:\n- recovered failures\n- a terminal failure after exhausting retries\n- a terminal failure with no retry\n\nNo gap or acknowledgment is needed.",
  "references": "0111ee261672ec1e98bf1a4371dc75cbab4ccd09f2da0a1899d1d980242d380e",
